  "id": "jamaican_dinki_mini_gerreh",
  "name": "Dinki mini and gerreh (Jamaican nine-night wake music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of Jamaican wakes, set-ups and nine-nights, the gatherings held on the nights after a death. Dinki mini, centred on St Mary and other eastern parishes, is a lively wake dance-song accompanied by drum, shakas, grater, katta sticks and the benta (a bamboo stick zither); gerreh is the related wake tradition of western parishes such as Hanover and Westmoreland. The membrane-drum card stands in for the drum, the shaker card for the shakas and the guayo (grater) card for the grater.",
  "recipe": "classic modern dinki mini and gerreh, funeral Lament, African diasporic branch, Caribbean groove percussion tumba francesa congo. single leader group response. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, shaker source guayo source unspecified. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
